# OpenSolar kernel manifest — ordered fragments for kernel-gen.sh.
# Format: <fragment-path-relative-to-kernel/> | <requires>
#   requires = "always"  -> included in every assembly
#   requires = <component> -> included only when that component is selected
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

fragments/identity.md|always
fragments/memory.md|always
fragments/iron-rules.md|always
fragments/self-check.md|always
fragments/dod.md|always
fragments/checkpoints.md|always
fragments/lazy-load.md|always
fragments/rules-index.md|always
fragments/agents-base.md|always
fragments/announce.md|always
components/core-runtime.md|core-runtime
components/harness.md|harness
components/skills-md.md|skills-md
components/codex-bridge.md|codex-bridge
# Solar-Max is an opt-in project mode (off by default). It instructs Claude to
# cd into a personal ~/Solar-MAX project dir, so it must NOT load on a default
# install. Gated behind the solar-max component.
fragments/solar-max.md|solar-max
